.TH TOKDUMP 1 "September 2026" "tokdump" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tokdump \- dump tokens (like hexdump, for tokens)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tokdump
[\fIfile\fR ...]
.br
.B tokdump
[\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR]
.br
.B tokdump
[\fB\-v\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tokdump
dumps token IDs for files or standard input using OpenAI's
.B o200k_base
encoding (the encoding used by GPT\-4o and related models), in a classic
three\-column hexdump\-C style layout.
.PP
With no files,
.B tokdump
reads standard input and dumps tokens.
With one or more files, it dumps each file; with more than one file, it prints
a header line
.BI tokdump: " FILENAME" :
before each dump.
.PP
Unreadable files produce an error on stderr, other files continue, and
the exit status is non\-zero if any file failed.
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
Each dump line has:
.TP
.B Offset
Token index as 7 lowercase hex digits.
.TP
.B Token IDs
Exactly 4 per row (last row may have fewer), each right\-aligned in width 7.
.TP
.B Text column
Starts at column 52. Spaces become
.BR · ,
newlines become
.BR ↵ ,
and other non\-printables become
.BR . .
.PP
After all tokens, a trailing line prints the next offset alone.
Empty input prints only
.BR 0000000 .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit 0.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version
.RB ( "tokdump <version>" )
and exit 0.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Dump tokens from stdin:
.B echo \-n "Hello world" | tokdump
.TP
Dump tokens in one file:
.B tokdump README.md
.TP
Dump tokens in multiple files:
.B tokdump a.txt b.txt
.SH ENCODING
v1 always uses
.BR o200k_base .
A future
.B \-e
/
.B \-\-encoding
flag may select other encodings.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hexdump (1),
.BR od (1),
.BR tc (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Omar Bohsali
